// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL2_3_Deadlock_PersonalStory_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P1504277138" "Deadlock's File"
// tDetailString :
"P3263663613" "After hearing Eagle Eye tell the story about how Back Alley Brawler was attacked by the man named Deadlock. You did some research on him and found a file 200 pages thick. In it you learned, among other things, that to Deadlock, killing is...<br><br><color DeepskyBlue><b>Nothing Personal, Just Business</b></color><br><br>They call him Deadlock - The man no prison can hold. He was hired by Veles Petrovic to take out Back Alley Brawler and protect The Skulls' ambitions for Kings Row. But Deadlock was in it for more than just the money. He had a history with Back Alley Brawler and twenty-three years of grudge that needed scratching. He left Brawler alive, but broken both physically and psychologically.<br><br>Maybe that was his plan all along..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - EagleEyeDialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P67814270" "From what I gathered from Brawler, it all started when Deadlock found a way past the security systems into Fort Trident..."
// Answer Text :
"P660707668" "Oh, that doesn't sound good... (Enter Mission)"
// Answer Text :
"P3982615850" "Hold that thought for one moment... (Leave)"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3315690086" "<color orange>A thought suddenly darkens Eagle Eye's demeanor as he reflects on events internally. Finally he chooses to speak on them.</color><br><br>I'm afriad I haven't been one-hundred percent forthcoming with information, {HeroName}. It's just, well, I didn't want to alarm you.<br><br>Back Alley Brawler should be the one who is congratulating you for taking down Veles and the Skulls' Superadine Lab. Unfortunately, he couldn't.<br><br>You see, Brawler was investigating the sudden surge in Superadine on the street himself. But when the Skulls caught wind of him snooping around their turf, the Petrovics decided to hire on some outside help to take care of him: a contract killer named Deadlock.<br><br>Deadlock and the Regulators go way back. He's a high priced killer and drug lords have a lot of money, so you can imagine that we had run ins with him from time to time.<br><br>Deadlock put Brawler in the hospital. If you like I can tell you all about it...<br><br><color yellow>This mission is a Single Player Mission only.</color>"
// AcceptString :
"P1186224649" "Is Brawler ok?"
// SendOffString :
"P1010322660" "His pride is about as crippled as he is, but he's going to make a full recovery.<br><br>When I heard this from Brawler I knew that the Skulls were up to something big here in Kings Row. I dusted off my old costume and carried on where Michael couldn't.<br><br>Here, I'll tell you all about it."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P504881809" "Deadlock's Personal Story<br>(Solo Mission)"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1844934631" "Listen well, you may run into Deadlock yourself one day."
// TaskTitle :
"P885016002" "<color deepskyblue>Deadlock's Personal Story</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P105911805" "<color deepskyblue>Nothing Personal, Just Business</color>"

